@meta
id: 04-08
title: Drill — read the number, jump, edit
chapter: 04
type: drill
skills: count-prefix, relativenumber
par: 23
minutes: 5
reps: 10
vscode: Ctrl-F, type FIXME, Escape, click
open: order.provider.ts
vimrc: set relativenumber

@brief
Ten times: put the ticket number on the FIXME comment. Append ` (ORD-418)`
— a space, then the bracketed id — to the end of that comment line.

Eyes find the comment, the margin gives you the distance, your hand types
the count. Do not count lines yourself, do not press `j` twice, and do not
touch an arrow key — twenty-nine lines of it is exactly the habit this
chapter is here to break.

@keys
| `29j` | down twenty-nine lines |
| `A` | append at the end of the line |

@hints
The margin already says how far it is. You are only reading a number off
the screen.
--
Read, jump, edit. Three moments. If any rep has a fourth, you moved twice
and the rep does not count.

@solution
    29j A  (ORD-418) <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Nineteen keystrokes, ten of them the ticket id.

By the last rep you should notice something odd and good: you stop
reading the number consciously. The margin says 29, your fingers type
`29j`, and no number goes through your head on the way. That is the point
at which relative numbers start paying for themselves, and it takes about
this many repetitions to arrive.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    // FIXME refunds are not idempotent yet
    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    // FIXME refunds are not idempotent yet (ORD-418)
    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}
